-- 7. SEED PRACTICAL FAQS FOR NYAYASETU
INSERT INTO faqs (id, right_id, question, answer) VALUES
(101, 101, 'Can an ICC refuse to accept an anonymous POSH complaint?', 'While the Act contemplates written complaints from the aggrieved woman, guidelines clarify that if an anonymous complaint contains verifiable specific evidence, the employer can initiate an administrative fact-finding inquiry.'),
(102, 102, 'Can an employer reduce my salary after returning from maternity leave?', 'No. Section 12 of the Maternity Benefit Act strictly prohibits any disadvantageous alteration in terms of service on account of maternity absence.'),
(201, 201, 'Can my company hold back my salary because client payment was delayed?', 'No. Under the Payment of Wages Act, payment of wages is an unconditional statutory obligation of the employer, irrespective of their third-party client contracts.'),
(501, 501, 'Can a builder force me to take possession if the Occupancy Certificate is not issued?', 'No. Offering possession without a valid Occupancy Certificate (OC) is illegal under RERA. You are entitled to interest on delay until valid OC is delivered.'),
(701, 701, 'Can an e-commerce platform print "No return, no refund" on invoices?', 'No. Under the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules 2020, blanket no-refund clauses for defective or mismatched goods constitute unfair trade practices and are legally void.'),
(801, 801, 'How fast must I call 1930 to stop an unauthorized bank transaction?', 'Within the first 1 to 2 hours (the "Golden Hour"). Immediate reporting allows the National Cyber Crime portal to place an instant freeze on the recipient bank account.'),
(901, 901, 'What is the maximum time a government department has to reply to an RTI query?', '30 calendar days normally. However, if the information concerns the life or liberty of a person, it must be provided within 48 hours under Section 7(1).'),
(1001, 1001, 'Do women have to show income proof to get free legal aid from DLSA?', 'No. Under Section 12(c) of the Legal Services Authorities Act 1987, all women and children are eligible for free legal aid regardless of their income level.'),
(1101, 1101, 'Can a senior citizen file a maintenance case against a grandson?', 'Yes. If the senior citizen has no surviving children, or if grandchildren are major heirs in possession of or set to inherit the ancestral estate.'),
(1401, 1401, 'Can a police station turn me away because the crime happened in another city?', 'No. The Supreme Court in Lalita Kumari held that police MUST register a Zero FIR immediately and subsequently transfer the investigation to the jurisdictional station.')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
